  "summaries": [
    {
      "id": 399773,
      "category": "team",
      "content": "A vulnerability in the privateDecrypt() API of the crypto library, allowed a covert timing side-channel during PKCS#1 v1.5 padding error handling.\n\nThe vulnerability revealed significant timing differences in decryption for valid and invalid ciphertexts. \n\nThis poses a serious threat as attackers could remotely exploit the vulnerability to decrypt captured RSA ciphertexts or forge signatures, especially in scenarios involving API endpoints processing Json Web Encryption messages.",
